    "simple": "A Baptist farmer of Low Hampton, New York, who from 1831 preached that Daniel’s 2,300 days would end “about the year 1843.” This desk indexes William Miller wherever the course cites that life, office, or published witness on the historicist timeline—not as an infallible authority on every disputed detail.",
    "history": "War of 1812 captain; published Evidence from Scripture and History… About the Year 1843 (Boston, 1842). He treated the metals as one chain and the earth as the sanctuary to be cleansed by fire. He did not invent 22 October — Samuel S. Snow did, at Exeter in August 1844. The Millerites made the earth the sanctuary. Hebrews will not let you. Open 9:23–24 next. 1818 + 25 years is “about 1843,” the range on his 1842 title page, Evidence from Scripture and History of the Second Coming of Christ, About the Year 1843. This sitting keeps his year-day arithmetic and refuses his event (the earth as sanctuary).",
