  "exile": {
    "simple": "The forced displacement of Judah to Babylon under God's judicial sentence across three deportations: 605, 597, and 586 B.C. Gold-linked terms open this card when the lesson needs the idea for dates, symbols, sanctuary themes, or rival schools (historicism, preterism, futurism).",
    "history": "Exile was not a chosen journey or a mere accident of war. Daniel 1:2 declares that the Lord handed Jehoiakim over to Nebuchadnezzar. Daniel and the first temple vessels leave in the 605 B.C. levy under Jehoiakim; Ezekiel and ten thousand more go in the 597 B.C. levy under Jehoiachin; the city and Solomon’s temple fall in the 586 B.C. levy under Zedekiah (2 Kings 24–25). Open Scripture to Daniel 1:2 and mark the verb gave. The sitting stands or falls on that word. Judah counts accession differently from Babylon. Jehoiakim’s third year in Daniel 1:1 and his fourth in Jeremiah 25:1 are the same campaign year, 605 B.C. Do not move the book to 586 to ‘fix’ the verse.",
    "proof": [
      "Scripture (KJV): Daniel 1:2 — sovereign hand in the first levy.",
      "Scripture (KJV): 2 Kings 24–25 — second and third levies under Jehoiachin and Zedekiah.",
      "Sitting 1 verify dock — 605 / 597 / 586 sequence.",
      "Scripture (KJV): Daniel 1:2 — verify in bible/kjv.json and the lesson Scripture dock."
    ]
  },
