    "history": "Dura is the type of forced worship; Revelation 13 is its global antitype. The earthly Day of Atonement is the type; Daniel 8:14 is the antitype in heaven. A type is not a metaphor you invent. It is a pattern Scripture itself repeats. In historicist reading, typology usually affects how you count time, match symbols to empires, or weigh preterist and futurist alternatives—follow the lesson sentence that linked the term before treating this card as settled. Re-read the Daniel references named in this card beside the sitting paragraph that first drove the conclusion; Scripture interprets Scripture before outside historians are invoked. Open the verify dock on any sitting where this term is linked in gold.",
